      "claim": "Direct L1 absolute/systemic F measurements for acidic or highly ionized reference molecules are at or above the 20% threshold: neotame at least 34.3% in fasted healthy volunteers, 6-MNA 35-38% in healthy subjects, and tolfenamic acid 91-100% in cirrhosis patients.",
      "card_ids": ["C15","C07","C11","C02","C12"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 fraction-absorbed records show carboxylic acid-containing molecules are well absorbed despite ionization at physiological pH: naproxen 98-100%, ketoprofen 100%, fenoprofen readily absorbed, and aspirin complete absorption from solution.",
      "card_ids": ["C47","C51","C53","C44","C46","C48","C49","C45","C52"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L5 gut-wall efflux records show acidic/zwitterionic reference molecules have efflux ratios near 1 and are not P-gp/BCRP substrates, with high bidirectional permeability in Caco-2 or intestinal models; no L5 record provides affirmative gut-wall efflux or intestinal-metabolism liability for the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C62","C58","C65","C61","C56","C57","C60","C54","C55","C63","C64"]
    },
